A||||11||Eddie||My sunroof is killng me||||8||
Z||000000||Eddie||12-14-1999||07:49 PM||||its making noise but its note leaking yet can it be fixed if so how (itS a stock sun roof) please help EDDIE||||reg||8
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||12-14-1999||08:35 PM||||I asume you mean wind-noise? Did you check the condition of the rubbers? Also check the two metal thingies on the front of the sunroof. If they are a bit bend out of shape, it will cause the sunroof to be lifted a bit - which in turn causes wind-noise.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric||12-14-1999||10:49 PM||||If his sunroof is anything like mine, than the air leak/ wind noise is coming from the back of the sunroof.  A new upper seal is going to be expensive.  Fierostore wants about $70 for a replacement.  I'm not even sure if that would solve the problem.  I was thinking an air deflector over thefront of the sunroof might quiet things down a little more.  They're only about $20-30.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sage||12-14-1999||10:57 PM||||Just a thought.  Make sure the glass is seated properly into the front of the opening.  It may look fine, but open it and make sure it is pushed all the way forward. Also as was allready mentioned, check the slide in clips, if they are bent they won't let the glass seat right.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||11:12 PM||||The slide in clips are supposed to be covered in vinyl.  If they aren't (mine weren't) replace them and the plastic washers that go with them.  They're about $13US total at the dealer.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||12-15-1999||06:28 AM||||Are you talking about wind noise or squeaking/rattling?||||reg||1
Z||000006||JetroGT||12-15-1999||04:00 PM||||If it's rattling when the sunroof is up then it's probably the two rubber washers that fit on the two pins of the handle. I replaced them on the SE and now it's quite.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Eddie||12-15-1999||06:10 PM||||its note wind noise its rattling and squeaking hay thanks for all the input EDDIE||||reg||6
Z||000008||william_thorniii||12-15-1999||06:51 PM||||Jetro,<P>These washers you are talking about are on the pin that the rear latch part pivots on right?  If so I think you just found my sunroof rattle.  <P>Let me know,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000009||JetroGT||12-16-1999||05:00 AM||||That's correct. It's the part that locks into the lactch.||||reg||14
Z||000010||Carrolles||12-16-1999||07:00 AM||||I replaced all the bolts (with the integral washers) that mount the hardware to the glass panel.  I also replaced the metal tabs (we'll call them hinges for this discussion) that slide into the holes at the front edge of the roof opening.  The plastic coating had cracked and fallen off of mine.  I got all new hardware from the dealer for less than $20.00 US.  It sure tightened up my sunroof.  I also got an extra spacer to tighten up the latch mechanism but didn't need it.<P>If that doesn't solve the problem than you might have to remove the headliner and see if the bolts that hold the sunroof frame to the roof structure have worked loose.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Voyd||12-16-1999||08:34 AM||||oh man, this has helped me alot. mine rattles even  when closed and has really bad wind noise, although it doesnt leak. when i replace my headliner soon i will definately shut that sunroof up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
